       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is double the maximum labeled dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould you check what was intended? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, or a different frequency.\n- Another dose that I should know about, with a note explaining why it exceeds the usual maximum.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away."
